# Button colors

Buttons use the brighter blue (`BLUE`, `(24, 92, 184)`).

Dark navy (`NAVY`, `(18, 36, 58)`) is only for a button that is currently deselected in a choice. The passphrase keyboard modes (`abc`, `ABC`, `.?123`, `#+=`) use it: the selected mode is brighter blue, and the others are navy.

A disabled button is grey, not navy. The title bar, toasts, and the boot screen may stay navy; those are not buttons.
